{# #188 -- app-wide footer, centered/stacked treatment (Raven's pick from
     3 mocked options, 2026-09-23): the mountain mark alone (no wordmark --
     that's the brand header's job, not this), a link row, then the
     copyright line beneath in smaller muted text. In normal document flow
     -- no position: fixed/sticky -- so it sits at the end of whatever
     content precedes it and scrolls away with the page, never pinned to
     the viewport. Included once, in app-layout.njk after its own main
     content block, rather than per-page: help-layout.njk itself chains
     through app-layout.njk (its own front matter sets layout:
     app-layout.njk), so this one include covers every owned app page AND
     every /help page with no second copy needed.

     2026-09-24 -- this comment used to name that content variable using
     Nunjucks' own real double-curly-brace output syntax, spelled out
     literally, in prose. Nunjucks has no notion of "this text is inside
     an HTML comment, don't evaluate it" -- it template-substitutes
     everywhere, so that literal expression was a second, live reference
     to the real content variable, rendered HTML-escaped (not marked safe
     here) and dumped into this comment on every single page that
     includes this file. Found via a real 3G-throttling investigation
     (Raven, 2026-09-24): it was roughly HALF of every page's total
     transferred bytes (/log: 51.6KB of 99.7KB; /help: 19.8KB of 41.1KB;
     /map: 11.1KB of 25.2KB), on every load. Never spell out Nunjucks'
     own output/tag delimiters literally in prose anywhere in a template
     file, comment or not -- describe them in words instead, the way this
     paragraph now does.

     Same mountain-mark SVG paths as climbing-header.js's own brand logo
     (kept in sync by hand -- copied exactly, not re-derived, same
     "pixel-identical to the real mark" precedent public/-/index.html's
     own values got when climbing-header.js's shared tokens were first
     extracted). max-w-[960px] mx-auto matches every page's own content
     column width, so the footer's centered content lines up under it
     rather than spanning the full viewport. #}
<footer class="max-w-[960px] mx-auto mt-16 pt-8 pb-4 border-t border-border flex flex-col items-center gap-4 text-center">
  <svg class="w-[1.4rem] h-[1.1rem] text-foreground" viewBox="0 14.4 122.88 96" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M45.6,14.4l23.718,48l-2.99,6l-21.689,0l10.843,21.6l-10.142,20.4l-45.342,0l45.6,-96Z" fill="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M85.203,37.2l16.333,31.2l-10.787,21.6l21.63,0l10.501,20.4l-74.042,0l36.364,-73.2Z" fill="currentColor"></path>
  </svg>
  <nav class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-[.85rem]" aria-label="Footer">
    <a class="text-foreground hover:text-accent" data-apex-link href="/help/">Help</a>
    <a class="text-foreground hover:text-accent" data-apex-link href="/help/ethics-and-sustainability/">Ethics &amp; sustainability</a>
    <a class="text-foreground hover:text-accent" data-apex-link href="/help/report-an-issue/">Report an issue</a>
    <a class="text-foreground hover:text-accent" data-apex-link href="/help/feedback/">Tell us what you think</a>
  </nav>
  <p class="text-[.78rem] text-muted">© {{ copyrightYear }} Nix Crabtree</p>
</footer>
